course: dictionary
lesson: 9354
title: Splint: a word for helping an injury
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A splint is a straight, stiff piece of wood, plastic or metal. It is tied to a broken or hurt arm, leg or finger to keep it still.
explain: Splint can also be a verb: to splint a finger means to put a splint on it. Look for clues like stiff, tied and keep still. Those clues tell you a splint is a support, not a sweet or a toy.
explain: «His little sister's fingers were stuck in the hinge, and she needed hospital and a splint.» Ask: what would fit here? Something that keeps a hurt finger still until a doctor can help. Try it: she needed hospital and a stiff support for her finger. It makes sense, so splint fits.
fact: A splint is a straight, stiff support for a hurt arm, leg or finger.
fact: «Put on a splint» means to fix a splint to an injured body part.
fact: «In a splint» means wearing a splint while an injury is cared for.
fact: «Finger splint» means a splint for a hurt finger.
fact: A splint can also be a thin strip of wood, so always check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
exercise: «The nurse put a splint on his broken arm.» What is a splint? | A sharp piece of glass | A cold drink for a sore throat | *A straight, stiff support that keeps a hurt part still | A soft bandage for a small cut
exercise: «Ruby's broken finger was splinted by the doctor.» Find and copy the word that means put a splint on. | doctor | broken | Ruby's | *splinted
exercise: Why does a splint stop a broken bone from moving? | *It keeps the bone still until a doctor can help | It hides the bone under the skin | It tickles the skin so the person laughs | It makes the bone grow faster
test: «He wore a finger splint for two weeks.» What is a finger splint? | *A small, stiff support for a hurt finger | A kind of finger puppet | A gold ring worn on the finger | A tiny pencil
test: Which phrase means wearing a splint while an injury heals? | under the bed | *in a splint | on the floor | out of the house
exam: Which of these is a splint with its thin strip of wood meaning? | *A thin, flat strip of wood | A bandage for a cut | A bruise on the knee | A cold drink
